<article class="demo-card demo-card--segmented" data-segmented-nav>
    <div>
        <p class="demo-label">Variation</p>
        <h2>Segmented Workspace Navigation</h2>
        <p class="demo-copy">A compact product-style nav that swaps the visible workspace panel inline.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="workspace-shell">
        <nav class="workspace-nav" aria-label="Segmented workspace navigation demo">
            <button class="workspace-nav__item is-active" type="button" data-workspace-nav-item>
                Overview
            </button>
            <button class="workspace-nav__item" type="button" data-workspace-nav-item>
                Analytics
            </button>
            <button class="workspace-nav__item" type="button" data-workspace-nav-item>
                Billing
            </button>
            <button class="workspace-nav__item" type="button" data-workspace-nav-item>
                Settings
            </button>
        </nav>

        <section class="workspace-panel workspace-panel--show" data-workspace-panel>
            <span class="workspace-panel__eyebrow">Overview</span>
            <h3>Everything important in one glance</h3>
            <p>Daily activity, release status, and last deployment summary sit together in the default panel.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="workspace-panel" data-workspace-panel>
            <span class="workspace-panel__eyebrow">Analytics</span>
            <h3>Watch trends as they move</h3>
            <p>Use compact navigation when the user needs to jump quickly between adjacent reporting views.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="workspace-panel" data-workspace-panel>
            <span class="workspace-panel__eyebrow">Billing</span>
            <h3>Payment state without leaving context</h3>
            <p>Invoices, renewal date, and seat usage can stay local to the same surface instead of opening a new page.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="workspace-panel" data-workspace-panel>
            <span class="workspace-panel__eyebrow">Settings</span>
            <h3>Configuration with minimal chrome</h3>
            <p>Segmented nav works well for settings groups when the information architecture is shallow.</p>
        </section>
    </div>
</article>